//!
//! @mainpage VCSC Toolchain
//!
//! @brief Developer documentation for the VCSC compiler toolchain.
//!
//! The tree is organized around small command-line tools that hand off plain
//! intermediate artifacts: vcsc-cc1 compiles `.c26` source to assembly, vcsc-as
//! assembles source to Intel HEX or o26 objects, vcsc-ld links o26 inputs,
//! vcsc-ar packages object archives, and vcsc coordinates the tools for
//! normal command-line use. Runtime support code and the simulator live beside
//! those tools because they are installed or used by end-to-end builds, but the
//! public tool modules below are the primary entry points for maintainers.
//!
//! User guides:
//! - @ref tool_usage
//!
//! Tool modules:
//! - @ref compiler
//! - @ref assembler
//! - @ref linker
//! - @ref archiver
//! - @ref driver
//!
//! Supporting modules:
//! - @ref runtime
//! - @ref simulator
//!
//! @defgroup compiler Compiler
//! @brief Sources for vcsc-cc1, including parsing, semantic checks, ABI metadata,
//! AST transforms, and assembly emission.
//!
//! @defgroup assembler Assembler
//! @brief Sources for vcsc-as, including lexer/parser glue, instruction
//! selection, relaxation, symbol management, listings, Intel HEX, and o26
//! object emission.
//!
//! @defgroup linker Linker
//! @brief Sources for vcsc-ld, including o26/archive loading, configuration,
//! relocation, layout, map output, and ABI metadata validation.
//!
//! @defgroup archiver Archiver
//! @brief Sources for vcsc-ar, the simple VCSL26 archive reader/writer used by
//! the linker.
//!
//! @defgroup driver Driver
//! @brief Sources for vcsc, the orchestration front-end that invokes the
//! compiler, assembler, linker, and archiver with installed search paths.
//!
//! @defgroup runtime Runtime support
//! @brief Runtime headers and support sources used by compiled programs.
//!
//! @defgroup simulator Simulator
//! @brief Simulator support used by vcsc-sim for end-to-end execution checks.
